course: dictionary
lesson: 9033
title: Slap: a hit, a sound, or a quick put-down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slap has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one to use. To slap is to hit someone or something with an open hand. In «She slapped the book on the desk», slapped means something else: she put the book down quickly and noisily.
explain: Check the clues. The words «on the desk» show that the book was put down, not hit. Try your meaning in the sentence: "She hit the book on the desk" does not quite fit what happened, so slapped here means put down quickly.
explain: Slap can also be a feeling word. In stories, a slap often shows anger or shock. In real life, slapping someone hurts them, and it is never OK. If someone slaps you, or you see it happen, tell an adult you trust straight away.
explain: Slap can also mean exactly or directly, as in «slap in the middle». In sport, a high five is a friendly slap of open hands. Context tells you which meaning is right every time.
fact: Slap means to hit with an open hand, and a slap is the hit itself.
fact: Slap can also mean to put something down quickly and noisily, as in «She slapped the book on the desk».
fact: Slap can mean exactly or directly, as in «slap in the middle».
fact: Slapping someone hurts them and is never OK: use words, and get help from an adult.
fact: Phrases with slap include slap on the back, slap your knee, slap on (put on quickly) and slap in the face.
exercise: «She slapped the book on the desk.» What does slapped mean here? | Opened very gently | Hid under her coat | Read slowly and quietly | *Put down quickly and noisily
exercise: «After the goal, the players gave each other a high five.» What is a high five? | A loud shout for a foul | *A friendly slap of open hands | A long, quiet hug | A kick with the foot
exercise: «Tom slapped on his coat and ran out of the door.» What does slapped on mean here? | Tore into pieces | *Put on quickly | Washed thoroughly | Took off slowly
test: «The arrow landed slap in the middle of the target.» What does slap in the middle mean? | Under the table | Broken into pieces | *Exactly in the middle | Near the edge
test: If someone slaps you, what should you do? | Keep it secret and hope it stops | *Tell an adult you trust straight away | Slap them back to show you are not scared | Laugh it off and say nothing
exam: In a story, «the king gave his guard a slap across the face» most likely shows what feeling? | *Anger or shock | Happiness at a party | Tiredness, like a yawn | Hunger
